; Per-head positional counts: the `(head :name … :min … :max …)` spelling
; of `:heads`.
;
; A head-set says *which* heads a slot accepts. On a form's `:positional`
; slot (the one place a head has a repeated population) it can also say
; *how many*. The compact `:names [a b c]` spelling cannot: the two
; spellings are mutually exclusive, so declaring one bound means writing
; every head as a `(head …)` child.
;
; Three bounds appear below, and the floor defaulting to 0 is the thing to
; read carefully:
;
;   :min 1 :max 1   exactly one
;   :max 1          at most one, none is fine
;   (no bound)      any number, including none
;
; A SECOND level of count sits on the set itself: `:min-children` /
; `:max-children`, how many children of *any* head in the set the slot
; holds. `(bgl-entry …)` below is the shape that needs it: a
; `GPUBindGroupLayoutEntry` binds exactly one resource, and no per-head
; spelling can say so. "at most one buffer AND at most one sampler" is
; satisfied by one of each, and by none at all.
;
; The two levels are independent claims and both are declared there:
; `:max 1` per head ("not two of the same") and `:min-children 1
; :max-children 1` over the set ("exactly one, whichever"). When they
; overlap, the validator suppresses the set's report in favour of the
; head's, because the per-head diagnostic names the line to delete.
;
; Two shapes here exist to pin what the counts *don't* do:
;
;   * `(section-holder :section …)` reuses `pipeline-section` on a KEYED
;     slot, where the bounds are inert: a keyed slot holds one value, so
;     `:max 1` is trivially satisfied and `:min 1` has no set to be
;     missing from. Inert rather than rejected, so a bounded kind stays
;     shareable between a slot with a population and one without.
;   * `(scratch-pipeline …)` is `:open true` with the same bounded slot.
;     Openness widens the *keyword* surface; it does not turn the counts
;     off. A form that declares `:positional <bounded-kind>` opted in.
;
; Export side: JSON Schema renders the counts as one `contains` +
; `minContains` / `maxContains` per bounded head, in the `$children`
; array's `allOf` beside the whole-set `items` union. Not
; `minItems`/`maxItems`; those bound the array's total length, which says
; nothing about how many children carry any one head. The set's bound is
; one more entry in the same `allOf`, whose `contains` is the `anyOf` of
; the members'. A floor at either level also puts `$children` in
; `required`, because the JSON bridge omits the key entirely for a
; childless form and `minContains` would have nothing to judge.
; TypeScript cannot express a per-member array count at all, so the
; `.d.ts` carries the bounds as a doc comment and nothing more.
(plugin :name head-counts :version "1.0.0"
  :description "Reference plugin for positional counts on a head-set, per head and over the whole set."

  (form :name vertex
    :description "The vertex stage of a pipeline."
    (key :name entry :type symbol :optional false))

  (form :name fragment
    :description "The fragment stage. Optional, because a depth-only pass has none."
    (key :name entry :type symbol :optional false))

  (form :name constant
    :description "A pipeline-overridable constant. Any number of these."
    (key :name name  :type symbol :optional false)
    (key :name value :type number :optional false))

  (value-kind :name pipeline-section
    :description "One section of a render pipeline, with how many of each are allowed."
    :underlying form
    :heads (head-set
      (head :name vertex   :min 1 :max 1 :description "The vertex stage. Exactly one.")
      (head :name fragment :max 1        :description "The fragment stage. At most one.")
      (head :name constant               :description "Pipeline-overridable constant. Any number.")))

  (form :name render-pipeline
    :description "A pipeline whose sections are counted, not just typed."
    :positional pipeline-section
    (key :name name :type symbol :optional false))

  (form :name section-holder
    :description "Same kind, keyed slot: the counts ride along inertly here."
    (key :name section :type pipeline-section :optional true))

  (form :name scratch-pipeline
    :description "Open form, same bounded slot: `:open true` does not silence the counts."
    :open true
    :positional pipeline-section)

  ; ---- the count over the whole set --------------------------------------

  (form :name buffer
    :description "A buffer binding."
    (key :name type :type symbol :optional false))

  (form :name sampler
    :description "A sampler binding."
    (key :name type :type symbol :optional false))

  (form :name texture
    :description "A texture binding."
    (key :name sample-type :type symbol :optional false))

  (value-kind :name bgl-resource
    :description "The one resource a bind-group-layout entry binds."
    :underlying form
    :heads (head-set :min-children 1 :max-children 1
      (head :name buffer  :max 1 :description "A buffer binding.")
      (head :name sampler :max 1 :description "A sampler binding.")
      (head :name texture :max 1 :description "A texture binding.")))

  (form :name bgl-entry
    :description "Exactly one resource: the claim per-head bounds cannot make."
    :positional bgl-resource
    (key :name binding :type number :optional false))

  ; The compact `:names` spelling carrying a set bound, which is legal on
  ; purpose: the aggregate needs no per-head metadata. A ceiling with no
  ; floor, so a `(data …)` with no generator is fine: the direction a
  ; `contains` without an explicit `minContains: 0` would get wrong.
  (value-kind :name data-shape-section
    :description "The one generator a (data …) may carry, if any."
    :underlying form
    :heads (head-set :names [cube sphere] :max-children 1))

  (form :name cube
    (key :name size :type number :optional false))

  (form :name sphere
    (key :name radius :type number :optional false))

  (form :name data
    :description "At most one generator: a ceiling-only set bound."
    :positional data-shape-section
    (key :name name :type symbol :optional false)))
